n Jen Kiggans and former Democratic Congresswoman Elaine Luria in a district with no partisan lean. The race sits among the most-watched House contests of 2026, with both campaigns focused on affordability and health care in Hampton Roads. Luria has raised about $4.7 million and holds a slight cash advantage, and Giffords PAC has put roughly $1 million behind her, while Kiggans has raised about $6 million as the incumbent.\n\nExpert raters split between Tossup and Lean D, with several calling it a likely Democratic flip, and prediction markets price Luria's chances near 80 percent. The only public poll, a July survey from a Democratic-leaning firm, showed the race tied. The forecast lands at a modest Democratic edge with wide uncertainty, consistent with a Lean D rating in a competitive district.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7963, "margin": 4.98}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8168, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.777, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7659, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.762, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7557, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.771, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7851, "margin": 4.5}]}